ed by the S/V split.", "3300": "Mis-tagged: prose rule (light cloth) with its closing title, not verse; 2-line block.", "3302": "Mis-tagged: prose closing line of the niḥsargika section, not verse; 1-line block.", "3353": "One rule (inserting, its listed examples, 'these are examples', closing title); 8 units kept as one point.", "3387": "Single offence between two others of the 'three doors of harm'; own paragraph.", "3410": "Dance, song and music: one group of three offences closed by one title; 7 units kept together.", "3466": "Unit carries an embedded bam-po marker (འདུལ་བའི་མདོ་བམ་པོ་དྲུག་པ།) before the rule text — likely should be split off as frame.", "3473": "Etiquette toward monks closing the 'contempt of superiors' group; 13-unit rule split in three where the topic turns.", "3516": "Section closing line stands alone.", "3526": "Section closing line stands alone.", "3531": "Vibhanga closing line stands alone; the general principles that follow (3532-3596) are grouped by topic.", "3597": "Closing line of the general-principles part stands alone.", "3670": "Chapter-part closing line stands alone.", "3689": "Chapter-part closing line stands alone.", "3713": "Conduct while carrying consent, 7 units on places and states to avoid; kept as one point.", "3734": "Chapter-part closing line stands alone.", "3749": "Lone-offender case with its scripted dialogue (3750-3753) kept together.", "3801": "Chapter-part closing line stands alone.", "3897": "Single rule on sweeping; own paragraph.", "3905": "Single rule on counting monks with tally-sticks; own paragraph.", "3928": "Closing line of the related-matters part stands alone.", "3929": "Closing line of the poṣadha chapter stands alone.", "3945": "Request and distribution of tally sticks split from the order of taking them (3947) and the counting (3951).", "3986": "Seven short rules kept together: one point, no reserving vihāras for particular persons.", "4004": "Announcement about mats; 4006 is the quotation close spli